// DD de-alias path LIB510 builds its per-frame section list as a run of interleaved NewPtr(8) section nodes +
// NewRgn regions out of the SAME contiguous low heap, so the host allocator packs each fresh region RIGHT
// BETWEEN two consecutive section nodes (node@3E4, rgn@3EC, node@3FC, rgn@404, ...) and RectRgn then writes a
// [-8000..8000] bbox over the node memory. Steering those regions off-heap (below) to break the overlap turns
// out to REGRESS DD (colors 201->1): the section builder REQUIRES node/region heap adjacency, and the actual
// distinct=1 stall is a corrupted COUNT field (obj+0x44 holds an end-POINTER, lives INSIDE the obj block and is
